Back-door candidates are common ancestors: collect each target's ancestors, then intersect.

```python
def common_causes(edges, t, y):
    def anc(n, seen):
        for a, b in edges:
            if b == n and a not in seen:
                seen.add(a)
                anc(a, seen)
        return seen
    return sorted(anc(t, set()) & anc(y, set()))
```

