Compare the two empirical CDFs at every observed value and keep the biggest gap.

```python
def ks_stat(a, b):
    if not a or not b:
        return 0.0
    cdf = lambda xs, v: sum(x <= v for x in xs) / len(xs)
    return max(abs(cdf(a, v) - cdf(b, v)) for v in a + b)
```

Equalized odds compares true-positive and false-positive rates across groups.

```python
def equalized_odds_gap(y, pred, group):
    def rate(g, label):
        p = [q for q, t, h in zip(pred, y, group) if h == g and t == label]
        return sum(p) / len(p) if p else 0.0
    gs = set(group)
    gap = lambda label: max(rate(g, label) for g in gs) - min(rate(g, label) for g in gs)
    return max(gap(1), gap(0))
```

